messages:
mina: dropped a fresh Figma pass for the 'abyss' dark theme — link: https://www.figma.com/file/yyy/abyss-theme

mina: Quick notes in the file: core bg #06070A, panel #0A0D10, code-surface #0B0F12. I'm worried about the saturation of the 'alert' red on small chart cells and the legibility of inline code tokens at 12px.

carlos: Saw it — love the deep tone. A few quick things: gridlines at alpha 0.14 on panels fail for small text. Also hover-only actions on the KPI cards — no keyboard focus currently.

jess: For code tokens i recommend moving away from high-yellow strings. Try #FFD08A -> too loud. Maybe #E6B86C or #DFA85A for warmth without causing bloom on token-bg. Keywords should be more desaturated blue, like #7AC4F0, so they read separate from links.

mina: Good call. Also thinking of using a muted magenta for types so function names don't clash with keywords: #C48BCF. But keep links as our standard teal (#66D6DA) so cross-product consistency remains.

sam: Ran Lighthouse and axe on the prototype: flagged issues — low contrast for tiny sparkline strokes, and tooltip triggers relying on mouseenter only.

carlos: For sparklines, increase stroke to 1.4px and set stroke-linecap round; raise opacity to 0.95. For tooltips add keyboard focus + aria attributes. aria-describedby for the tooltip content helps screen readers.

mina: Also: heatmap legend is color-only. We need a secondary encoding. Proposing three options in Figma: 1) diagonal hatch overlay for low buckets, 2) small dot density pattern, 3) append numeric label inside each bucket on hover/print. Which do you all prefer?

jess: I vote hatch overlay. It's compact and prints well. Make hatch subtle (1.5px lines at 45deg, 10px spacing). Also add a thin outline to each cell at alpha 0.06 to help in greyscale.

sam: Recommend we test deuteranopia and greyscale sims. Also set heatmap palette endpoints so the mid-tone isn't mistaken for background — try endpoint low #21323A -> mid #3E6B7A -> high #FF6A5A. Avoid pure neon reds.

mina: Dropping a CSS tokens snippet to use in the staging branch. I'll push soon.

mina: ```css
:root {
  --abyss-bg: #06070A;
  --abyss-surface: #0A0D10;
  --code-surface: #0B0F12;
  --text-1: #E8F0F3;
  --code-string: #DFA85A;
  --code-keyword: #7AC4F0;
  --code-type: #C48BCF;
  --link: #66D6DA;
  --heat-low: #21323A;
  --heat-mid: #3E6B7A;
  --heat-high: #FF6A5A;
}
```

carlos: Nice. Small UI nit: make focus rings 3px for high-contrast elements in dark mode (ring color #88E6FF at 0.95 opacity) so tabbing is obvious on dark backgrounds.

jess: And for code blocks, try `box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,0.02)` and `border-radius: 6px` — keeps them feeling lifted without adding a bright edge.

sam: Once you push, I'll re-run axe and the color blindness simulations. Please add a storybook variant with the hatch overlay so QA can toggle it.

mina: Will do. Pushing branch feat/abyss-theme now.

deploy-bot: build:staging queued by mina — branch feat/abyss-theme :rocket:

carlos: If staging passes, let's also add a small accessibility task to the sprint for keyboard tooltip fixes. Low lift but important.

mina: Agree. Thanks all — ping me if you want to pair on hatch tiling or the heatmap endpoints. :party:

ux-bot: Reminder: upload final token list to tokens repo after merge.
